# heavy_atom_to_C_ratio
# Feature description: The ratio of the number of heavy atoms (nHM) to the percentage of carbon atoms (C%).
# Usefulness: This feature captures structural complexity normalized by the carbon backbone, which may influence biodegradability through molecular stability and reactivity pathways.
df['heavy_atom_to_C_ratio'] = df['nHM'] / (df['C%'] + 1e-8)
end

---

#### 2. Aggregated Feature: Difference between spectral moments of Laplace and Burden matrices

python
# spectral_moment_diff
# Feature description: The difference between spectral moments of order 6 from the Laplace matrix (SM6_L) and Burden matrices weighted by mass (SM6_B(m)).
# Usefulness: Spectral moments describe molecular structure properties (e.g., connectivity and weight distribution). Their difference can highlight structural variations important for biodegradability.
df['spectral_moment_diff'] = df['SM6_L'] - df['SM6_B(m)']
end

---

#### 3. Nonlinear Transformation: Logarithm of sum of dO E-states

python
# log_SdO
